    hub: [
      "February begins in Aquarius' second decan, where Mercury as sub-ruler gives the sign a chatty, networked intelligence. Around February 9 the third decan arrives, and Venus warms Aquarian ideals with charm and a sense of fairness. Then, around February 18 or 19, the Sun enters Pisces, the last sign of the zodiac. The move is from fixed air to mutable water, from concept to feeling, and many people sense that late-February birthdays carry a softer, more porous quality. The final days of the month sit in Pisces' first decan, where Neptune is doubled and imagination runs freely. In leap years, February 29 falls just inside the second decan, where the Moon begins to shape the sign. The month as a whole traces a line from the mind's ideals to the heart's intuitions.",
      "Numerologically, February is month 2, the number of cooperation, diplomacy and quiet perception. It tends to temper whatever the rest of a birth date contributes with a wish to work alongside others. February is also the trickiest month for the Chinese zodiac. Lunar New Year can fall as late as February 20, so a birthday in the first half of the month may still belong to the previous year's animal, and it is worth checking the exact date for the year in question rather than assuming. From February 21 onwards, the new year has always begun. In Four Pillars astrology the Tiger month opens around February 4 with the solar term called the Beginning of Spring, so most February birthdays carry the Tiger's restless, courageous energy in the month pillar.",
    ],
